# Who may read or write what. "pattern" lines apply to every account; plain "topic" lines before
# the first "user" would apply to anonymous clients only (refused here).
# A device's account name is its id: it reads the buzzer state and writes only on its own topic
# (sentinel/<id>), so a compromised ESP can neither impersonate another one nor ring the siren.
# (mosquitto warns that this pattern has no %u: expected, it is the same topic for everyone.)
pattern read sentinel/cmd/buzzer
pattern write sentinel/%u

# The API: every measurement, and the commands.
user sentinel-api
topic read sentinel/+
topic write sentinel/cmd/#
